---
// Canonical rendering for TER's F̂ (perceived feasible set) in normal UI
// text. Renders a real "F" plus a manually positioned, non-combining
// circumflex glyph (U+02C6), sized in em so it scales with whatever
// context it's dropped into. Deliberately avoids a combining Unicode
// accent (unreliable at large display sizes on variable fonts) and
// avoids CSS border-triangle hats (drawn independently per component,
// and prone to clipping — see git history for both prior approaches).
---
<span class="fhat" aria-label="F hat">
  <span class="fhat-mark" aria-hidden="true">ˆ</span>F
</span>

<style>
  .fhat {
    position: relative;
    display: inline-block;
    padding-top: 0.28em;
  }

  .fhat-mark {
    position: absolute;
    top: 0.02em;
    left: 50%;
    font-size: 0.75em;
    line-height: 1;
    color: currentColor;
    transform: translateX(-50%);
  }
</style>
